ta","data":[{"unit":1,"title":3,"area":77,"prev":79,"next":82,"titles":84,"firmware":253},{"id":2,"title":3,"aliases":4,"area":10,"order":11,"path":12,"context":13,"summary":16,"status":17,"firmware":18,"facts":23,"procedures":43,"parameters":62,"related":63,"body":67,"sources":68,"official_url":27,"controls":74},"hardware.te-boot","TE boot (bootloader menu)",[5,6,7,8,9],"te boot","bootloader","boot menu","recovery menu","boot mode","hardware",60,"knowledge/manual/units/hardware/te-boot.md",{"modes":14,"screens":15},[],[5],"The bootloader menu, reached by holding `com` while switching on. `T1` installs firmware, `T7` factory-resets and `T8` opens the system menu with the key test; switching off and on leaves.","current",{"min":19,"changed_in":20,"guide_version":21,"verified_on":22},"1.0.9",[],"1.1.15",null,[24,29,33,36,39],{"id":25,"text":26,"source":27,"firmware_min":22,"verified_on":22,"confidence":28},"what","TE boot is the OP-XY's bootloader, the program that loads and starts its firmware.","https://teenage.engineering/downloads/op-xy","official",{"id":30,"text":31,"source":32,"firmware_min":22,"verified_on":22,"confidence":28},"jobs","Firmware updates, factory resets and hardware tests all run from TE boot rather than from the normal OS.","https://teenage.engineering/guides/op-xy/te-boot#te-boot",{"id":34,"text":35,"source":32,"firmware_min":22,"verified_on":22,"confidence":28},"enter","To reach it, switch the unit off, then keep `com` held while switching it back on.",{"id":37,"text":38,"source":32,"firmware_min":22,"verified_on":22,"confidence":28},"menu","The TE boot screen offers three numbered choices, each picked with the track key of its number: firmware upload (1), factory reset (7) and the system menu (8).",{"id":40,"text":41,"source":42,"firmware_min":22,"verified_on":22,"confidence":28},"exit","Switching the unit off and on again leaves TE boot without changing anything.","https://teenage.engineering/guides/op-xy/te-boot#exiting-te-boot",[44,55],{"id":34,"goal":45,"preconditions":46,"steps":47,"result":54,"source":32,"firmware_min":22,"verified_on":22,"confidence":28},"Start the OP-XY in TE boot",[],[48,51],{"keys":49,"note":50,"set":22},"power","switch off",{"keys":52,"note":53,"set":22},"com + power","hold com while switching back on","The TE boot menu lists its three options.",{"id":40,"goal":56,"preconditions":57,"steps":58,"result":22,"source":42,"firmware_min":22,"verified_on":22,"confidence":28},"Leave TE boot",[],[59],{"keys":60,"note":61,"set":22},"power → power","off, then on again",[],[64,65,66],"hardware.firmware-update","hardware.factory-reset","hardware.system-menu","TE boot sits underneath the normal OS, so it is reachable even when the OS itself misbehaves.\nUpdating (`T1`) and resetting (`T7`) have their own units, and the system menu (`T8`) is for\nchecking faulty keys or recalibrating the volume knob.\n\nNothing in TE boot happens by accident: every action needs a track key, and a power cycle leaves.\nThis app never switches the unit into TE boot; you do it on the device.",[69,71,73],{"url":27,"kind":70},"te",{"url":32,"kind":72},"guide",{"url":42,"kind":72},[75,76],"switch.power","key.com",{"id":10,"title":78},"Hardware",{"id":80,"title":81},"hardware.specifications","Technical specifications",{"id":64,"title":83},"Updating the OS",{"basics.key-notation":85,"basics.main-modes":86,"basics.modules":87,"basics.track-buttons":88,"basics.linked-tracks":89,"basics.patterns-scenes-songs":90,"basics.workflow":91,"basics.firmware-versions":92,"hardware.layout":93,"hardware.power-and-charging":94,"hardware.connectors":95,"hardware.specifications":81,"hardware.te-boot":3,"hardware.firmware-update":83,"hardware.factory-reset":96,"hardware.system-menu":97,"hardware.safety-and-care":98,"hardware.in-the-box":99,"sequencer.overview":100,"sequencer.step-entry":101,"sequencer.step-recording":102,"sequencer.live-recording":103,"sequencer.extend-notes":104,"sequencer.nudge":105,"sequencer.single-sound":106,"seq